  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Right after that, Samsonov returns to Arkady in the hallway after his failed staring experiment. Arkady reassures him that Nina's dismissive reaction is completely normal psychological denial. He gives him instructions on how to say goodbye dramatically to his children before moving into the luxury hotel. Let's listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Рот закрой, Самсонов, продует!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты до десяти досчитал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "samson",
      "t": "Да, всё досчитал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ничего страшного, это логично.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это первая стадия — отрицание.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "samson",
      "t": "Чего? Какое отрицание?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не бери в голову.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Когда будешь уходить из дома...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не забудь поцеловать детей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Скажи: я навсегда ваш папа.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "samson",
      "t": "Понял, поцелую и скажу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "samson",
      "t": "А куда потом идти?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ко мне в гостиницу, Самсонов!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Там мы продолжим операцию.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's examine Arkady's strategic relationship coaching line by line. Arkady gives Samsonov precise behavioral advice in the hallway.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Рот закрой, Самсонов, продует!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Close your mouth, Samsonov, you'll catch a draft!' Arkady snaps at his flustered neighbor.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты до десяти досчитал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you count to ten?' Arkady asks if he followed the timed staring instructions.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "samson",
      "t": "Да, всё досчитал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I counted all of it.' Samsonov confirms that he completed the count.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ничего страшного, это логично.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Nothing terrible, that is logical.' Arkady uses a neuter short adjective to normalize the failure.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это первая стадия — отрицание.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is the first stage: denial.' The psychological concept refers to the stages of grief.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "samson",
      "t": "Чего? Какое отрицание?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What? What denial?' Samsonov is confused by the unfamiliar psychological terminology.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не бери в голову.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Don't worry about it.' The Russian idiom literally means 'do not take it into your head'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Когда будешь уходить из дома...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'When you are leaving home...' The compound future construction sets the timeframe.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не забудь поцеловать детей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Don't forget to kiss the children.' The negative imperative is followed by an infinitive.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Скажи: я навсегда ваш папа.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Say: I am always your dad.' Arkady scripts a melodramatic parting line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "samson",
      "t": "Понял, поцелую и скажу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Got it, I will kiss them and say it.' Samsonov agrees to deliver the scripted goodbye.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "samson",
      "t": "А куда потом идти?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And where do I go afterwards?' Samsonov asks about the practical destination.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ко мне в гостиницу, Самсонов!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'To my hotel, Samsonov!' Arkady directs him to his hotel headquarters.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Там мы продолжим операцию.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There we will continue the operation.' The plural future verb frames the plan as a political campaign. Now let's listen to Arkady and Samsonov's hallway conversation once more without pauses.",
